  {
   "id": 531058,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<p><img src=\"exercises/media/f5dcdd69ea3e9aba.jpg\" alt=\"The table has three columns, species, the birth rate in N per year, and the death rate in N per year.  For Species A, the birth rate was 1845 and the death rate was 1467. For Species B, the birth rate was 43 and the death rate was 79. For Species C, the birth rate was 2800 and the death rate was 21115. For Species D, the birth rate was 16 and the death rate was 16. For Species E, the birth rate was 933 and the death rate was 1351.\"></p>\n\n<p>The table contains birth rates and death rates for populations of several species living in the same ecosystem. \nAnalyze the data to identify the population(s) experiencing a negative change in population size.</p>\n",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1039548,
     "content_html": "species A only"
    },
    {
     "id": 1039549,
     "content_html": "species A and species C"
    },
    {
     "id": 1039550,
     "content_html": "species B and species D"
    },
    {
     "id": 1039551,
     "content_html": "species B and species E"
    }
   ],
